WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.222
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.522 --> 00:00:08.886
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.186 --> 00:00:15.333
Unit twenty-two: Cities and Transport. Today you will imagine changes with the second conditional.

4
00:00:15.633 --> 00:00:18.227
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:22.504
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:24.130
Urban.

7
00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:27.070
Urban means related to a city.

8
00:00:27.683 --> 00:00:29.834
Urban areas are growing fast.

9
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.777
Your turn. Say: Urban.

10
00:00:35.633 --> 00:00:36.402
Urban.

11
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:38.557
Public transport.

12
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:43.059
Public transport means buses and trains for everyone.

13
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.149
Public transport is cheaper than a taxi.

14
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:49.844
Your turn. Say: Public transport.

15
00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.073
Public transport.

16
00:00:54.817 --> 00:00:55.992
Traffic jam.

17
00:00:56.983 --> 00:00:59.854
Traffic jam means many cars stuck on a road.

18
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:03.007
We were stuck in a traffic jam for an hour.

19
00:01:03.617 --> 00:01:06.582
Your turn. Say: Traffic jam.

20
00:01:09.433 --> 00:01:10.655
Traffic jam.

21
00:01:11.417 --> 00:01:12.395
Bus lane.

22
00:01:13.383 --> 00:01:16.347
Bus lane means a part of the road only for buses.

23
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.484
The bus lane helps buses move faster.

24
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:22.631
Your turn. Say: Bus lane.

25
00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:26.595
Bus lane.

26
00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:28.119
Cycling.

27
00:01:29.117 --> 00:01:31.163
Cycling means riding a bicycle.

28
00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.633
Cycling is healthy and clean.

29
00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.891
Your turn. Say: Cycling.

30
00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:40.607
Cycling.

31
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:42.165
Planning.

32
00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.649
Planning means deciding how to design something.

33
00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.203
Good planning makes cities better.

34
00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:51.063
Your turn. Say: Planning.

35
00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:54.855
Planning.

36
00:01:55.617 --> 00:01:56.351
Commute.

37
00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.709
Commute means to travel to work or school.

38
00:02:00.317 --> 00:02:02.316
I commute by bus every day.

39
00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:05.151
Your turn. Say: Commute.

40
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:08.780
Commute.

41
00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:10.576
Sustainable.

42
00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:15.034
Sustainable means able to continue without harming the planet.

43
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.800
Electric buses are more sustainable.

44
00:02:18.417 --> 00:02:20.965
Your turn. Say: Sustainable.

45
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:24.987
Sustainable.

46
00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.428
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:33.583
Visal, how could transport in your city be improved?

48
00:02:34.683 --> 00:02:37.972
If there were more buses, there would be less traffic.

49
00:02:39.083 --> 00:02:40.351
What about cycling?

50
00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:45.957
If we had safe bike lanes, more students would cycle to school.

51
00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:48.179
And your commute?

52
00:02:49.283 --> 00:02:53.547
If there were a bus lane, my commute would be twenty minutes shorter!

53
00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.363
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:57.217 --> 00:02:59.390
Grammar focus: Second conditional.

55
00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:00.900
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:01.617 --> 00:03:04.313
If there were more buses, there would be less traffic.

57
00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:07.750
If we had bike lanes, more people would cycle.

58
00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:11.021
If I lived near school, I would walk.

59
00:03:11.967 --> 00:03:17.707
Use the second conditional for imagined situations now. Use 'were' for all subjects after 'if'.

60
00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:23.680
Be careful! Don't say: If there were more buses, there will be less traffic.

61
00:03:25.633 --> 00:03:29.119
Say: If there were more buses, there would be less traffic.

62
00:03:29.419 --> 00:03:32.057
The second conditional uses 'would' in the main clause.

63
00:03:32.867 --> 00:03:35.484
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:37.498
Moving Our City.

65
00:03:37.798 --> 00:03:40.135
Urban planning shapes how people commute.

66
00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:44.677
A good public transport system reduces traffic jams.

67
00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:48.537
If there were more bus lanes, buses would be faster.

68
00:03:49.533 --> 00:03:52.299
Safe cycling routes make cities more sustainable.

69
00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.228
If more people took the bus, the air would be cleaner.

70
00:03:57.333 --> 00:04:01.277
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:02.117 --> 00:04:05.057
If there were more buses, there blank be less traffic.

72
00:04:05.357 --> 00:04:08.244
A, would. B, will. C, are.

73
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.405
The answer is A: would.

74
00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:17.455
Many cars stuck on a road make a traffic blank.

75
00:04:17.755 --> 00:04:20.967
A, jam. B, lane. C, plan.

76
00:04:24.533 --> 00:04:26.672
The answer is A: jam.

77
00:04:27.817 --> 00:04:30.223
To travel to work or school is to blank.

78
00:04:30.523 --> 00:04:33.921
A, commute. B, cycle. C, plan.

79
00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:39.199
The answer is A: commute.

80
00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.563
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:47.252
How could transport in your city be improved?

82
00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:57.608
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:57.908 --> 00:05:05.599
If there were more buses and bike lanes, there would be less traffic. If people shared cars, the air would be cleaner.

84
00:05:05.899 --> 00:05:07.574
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:08.483 --> 00:05:12.285
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and second conditional.

86
00:05:12.585 --> 00:05:17.583
Today's value is sustainability. Choose ways of living that protect the planet for the future.

87
00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:21.603
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

88
00:05:21.903 --> 00:05:24.857
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

